haplo-dialog, Announcements for users
======================================

This file summarises the important changes from the user's point of view.
For the complete technical history, see CHANGELOG.md.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────
Version 1.0.0 (2026-05-29), First public release
──────────────────────────────────────────────────

haplo-dialog 1.0.0 is the first stable public release.

haplo-dialog is the modern, hardened and maintained successor to gtkdialog.
Describe an interface in XML, run it from the shell, retrieve the values
entered. Where gtkdialog is abandoned, haplo-dialog brings it back to life:
fixed, hardened, maintained.

* A single port: gtk3dialog, the reference GTK 3 backend. It implements
  43 widgets and is driven entirely in XML from the shell.

* gtkdialog backwards compatibility: installing gtk3dialog creates a
  "gtkdialog" alias, your legacy gtkdialog 0.8.x scripts run as is
  (XML, options and environment variables).

* Strengthened security: all commands go through safe_exec.
  No more direct calls to system() in the code. The parser cleanly rejects
  malformed XML, and the code is subjected to fuzzing.

* Binary hardening: _FORTIFY_SOURCE=3, PIE, Full RELRO,
  stack-protector-strong, -fcf-protection (depending on the compiler).

* Test suite: 52 XML regression cases and 9 behaviour tests (safe_exec).

* Packaging for Debian, Fedora, Arch, Gentoo, Slackware.

To install:

  # Debian / Ubuntu
  sudo apt install gtk3dialog

  # Arch Linux (from source)
  cd gtk3dialog/gtk3dialog_1.0.0/packaging/arch && makepkg -si

  # From source (autotools)
  cd gtk3dialog/gtk3dialog_1.0.0 && autoreconf -fi && ./configure && make && sudo make install

Documentation: https://haplo-dialog.fr
Bug reports: devel@haplo-dialog.fr
Security: devel@haplo-dialog.fr

──────────────────────────────────────────────────

